{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH their Elohim.</b> The reason He repeated this a second time — perhaps it intends to include even at a time when His Shekhinah is not among us, that He is YHWH our Elohim and to Him we belong. Or it may intend in this manner: through their knowledge and recognition of the matter, as He said at the outset, ״וְיָדְעוּ״ etc. — through this they are worthy of having My name called upon them, to call Him יהוה their Elohim; but without this they would cast off the yoke and turn to other elohim elsewhere."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:31.470101072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}